  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Breadboard hole positions estimated from the circuit image. The image labels the upper half rows j-f, while the catalogue names the upper half bank 't' with rows a-e; I mapped image rows f,g,h,i,j to catalogue rows a,b,c,d,e (so image row g = 'b', h = 'c', i = 'd'). Strips are the same either way.",
   "Rail hole numbers (tp.2, tn.4, tp.6, tn.13, tn.26) are approximate; each rail is one strip so connectivity is unaffected.",
   "Circuit: 5V -> photoresistor -> junction (A0) -> 10k resistor -> GND; pin 9 -> LED anode (long, bent leg), LED cathode -> 220 ohm resistor -> GND, as in the schematic.",
   "The Arduino GND wire goes to the GND pin next to the power header (GND.1).",
   "The text says 'Analog input 2' in a caption, but the circuit image, schematic and text use A0, so A0 is used.",
   "10k resistor value written as 10000 (ohms)."
  ]
 },
